{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - MFA - Potentially Successful Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications [table]",
	"Description": "The dangerous half of MFA fatigue: an account that denied or ignored several push prompts and then approved one. The approval at the end of a run of refusals is the moment the victim gave in, so unlike the plain MFA bombing detection this one implies the adversary is now inside.\n\nThresholds: 2 or more denied or ignored prompts and at least 1 success, per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune them.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_potentially_successful_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "d13558b2-a80a-59e2-8d06-cc6ed96df55f",
	"SearchReference": "6438b4a1-ccd5-56b3-8583-ff8a37be74f1"
